 "_comment": "Land-use class table (#253): tag mapping and per-class defaults together. No class ships a fence default (every boundary is null). Furniture (#260): park ships bench_per_100m (benches on its paths); every other class ships null. highways is the default lamp spacing in blocks along the way, staggered either side, per OSM highway class; a class absent here (service, path, cycleway, steps, links) is not lit by inference, and a district profile or street convention beats it. Surface (#316): surface.unmapped_paving is the kind aerial paving takes off a mapped way (dirt, grass, or null to keep the aerial paving); surface.path_widen (#325) is the reach in blocks (1..6, or null) beside a mapped path within which aerial paving takes that path's own surface, so a path the map draws thin reads as wide as the aerial shows it (park 3; every other class null). New per-class keys join land_use.OPTIONAL_COLUMNS. Pure reader: lib/sources/land_use.py. Plan: docs/plans/land-use-classes.md.",
